{"id": "striviaqa0205", "pool": "striviaqa", "tier": "balanced", "audio_s": 8.95, "n_chunks": 9, "n_concurrent": 9, "gen_active_at_eot": true, "eot_score": 0.2913, "eot_read_ms": 30, "reference_answer": "big brother (accepted aliases: big brother disambiguation, big brother song, big brother film, bigbrother1, big brother, big bruvva, bigbrother)", "query": "What is a reality TV show in which a group of people live in a large house watched by cameras, first broadcast in the Netherlands in 1999?", "transcript": "What is a reality TV show in which a group of people live in a large house watched by cameras, first broadcast in the Netherlands in one thousand nine hundred and ninety nine?", "mode": "local", "answer": "A reality TV show is a type of television program in which the events and actions of the participants are presented as they happen, often without scripted dialogue or staged scenarios. These shows typically involve a group of people living together in a shared environment—such as a house, a remote location, or even on a boat—while being filmed by cameras that capture their interactions, emotions, and daily lives. Reality TV can range from competition-based formats like cooking challenges or talent contests to more observational styles where viewers see how ordinary individuals navigate social dynamics, personal conflicts, or unique situations. Because the content feels \"real\" and unscripted, these shows aim to entertain by showcasing authentic human behavior, although producers may still influence outcomes through editing or behind-the-scenes direction. Popular examples include shows like Big Brother, Survivor, and Keeping Up with the Kardashians.", "answer_ms": 5507}
